===Etymology===
Via {{bor|en|fr|pastiche}}, from {{der|en|it|pasticcio||pie, something blended}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*pasticium}}, from {{der|en|la|pasta||dough, pastry cake, paste}}, from {{der|en|grc|παστά||barley porridge}}, from {{m|grc|παστός||sprinkled with salt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pæsˈtiːʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pastiche.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːʃ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[image:Pastiche.jpg|thumb|[[w:Botticelli|Botticelli]]'s original on the left, '''pastiche''' on the right. (1)]]

# A [[work]] of [[art]], [[drama]], [[literature]], [[music]], or [[architecture]] that [[imitate]]s the work of a [[previous]] [[artist]].
# A [[musical]] [[medley]], typically [[quote|quoting]] other works.
# An [[incongruous]] [[mixture]]; a [[hodgepodge]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[postmodern]] [[playwriting]] technique that fuses a variety of styles, genres, and story lines to create a new form.

